{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cold-censorable-armedcrab","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 11 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/store-history.args`, which this bug owns.\n\n`tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py` (3) restores nothing from tickets history, `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_repair_restore_08c8.py` (5) reports `rebuilt is False`, and `tests/unit/test_store_write_unmerged_recovery.py` (3) cannot create its `UU` fixture (`git ls-files -u` is empty). The fsck restore tests passed when run serially on Windows (run 44672240702: 5 passed) but fail under xdist (runs 44665461131 and 44681457334), so an interaction between tests is in play. Forcing `core.autocrlf=true` on macOS does not reproduce them.\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\nModules:\n- `tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py` (3)\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_repair_restore_08c8.py` (5)\n- `tests/unit/test_store_write_unmerged_recovery.py` (3)\n\n## Approach\nReproduce on a Windows runner with `-p no:randomly` and single-test runs to separate the interaction from a platform cause, then fix the class. Remove each line from `store-history.args` as it passes.\n\n## Scope\nTest or product code for the listed modules, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/store-history.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `store-history.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `store-history.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n","id":"a2da-e61b-989e-4862","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 11 store-history restore and unmerged-path tests fail; cause not yet established"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795154285311984001,"uuid":"f296f9fd-28d1-4ed1-bc1a-28aa560a0924"}